id: pm-web-maker-links
title: Credit the maker and unbrained in the public application footer
description: "Show a plain maker credit in the shipped application shell for hosted and self-hosted instances, using existing theme tokens."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-14T10:20:51.010Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T20:24:09.758Z"
author: codex-maker-links-1114
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T10:20:55.270Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Searched maker, footer and preu before creating this item. Add one static footer line to the package application shell, outside authentication-specific views, using existing theme tokens and native links. Verify the served markup, a behavioral revert, focused frontend checks and release gates, then regenerate and check the changelog. Leave delivery in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-14T10:23:41.990Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Focused linked tests passed 34/34 with no skips, including theme contrast, locale parity and replay privacy. Typecheck passed. Behavioral revert: restoring only the original application HTML makes the new footer test fail (1 pass, 1 fail); restoring the changed HTML passes 2/2. Broad validation uses a dedicated disposable test database, keeping other test runs isolated."
  "2026-11-14T10:26:45.100Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Static HTML served over a local HTTP preview changes both preu.at and unbrained.dev link counts from 0 to 1. Browser layout passed 12 combinations: phone, landscape and desktop viewports, both themes, authentication and application states; both links remain visible and hit-testable without horizontal overflow. The footer is plain package markup with existing theme tokens. Changelog regeneration and check passed without a content diff."
  "2026-11-14T11:17:49.218Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Full isolated npm release gate coverage suite finished 1008/1010 passing, one failure and one cancellation, zero skips. Failures reproduce the existing built-catalog 300000 ms timeout and subsequent source spawn ENOTDIR signature recorded in pm-web-qdhx. Focused footer/locale/contrast/privacy checks remain 34/34 passing; no tests or thresholds were weakened. Required Bun gate and independent downstream stages remain to be evaluated."
  "2026-11-14T11:22:17.197Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Independent downstream checks passed: npm run audit:prod reports zero vulnerabilities; verify:release-changelog-date and verify:release-publish-attestation pass. Full development audit reports the three moderate c8/test-exclude/glob findings already owned by pm-web-c8-glob-advisory, which now has the fresh receipt. Bun release gate is running sequentially after npm."
  "2026-11-14T12:07:57.111Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Both required full release attempts are terminal: npm and Bun each finish 1008/1010 passing, one failed catalog case and one timeout cancellation, zero skips, with unchanged thresholds. Both stop at coverage due the existing pm-web-qdhx signature. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication and documentation gates passed in both attempts. Independent capacity, dry-pack and packed-consumer checks are next; production audit and both release metadata guards already pass."
  "2026-11-14T12:17:31.344Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Independent downstream stages passed: npm run accept:capacity 2/2, npm run pack:dry-run 513 files, npm run accept:packed 4/4 (npm and Bun, current and minimum CLI hosts). Eight permission launchers pass; packed artifact SHA-256 1dbd2a1c7995cc36056c5645145cfdf042e7fb06a5cdab783260d88f778085a3. Production audit reports zero vulnerabilities; both release metadata guards pass. Both full release chains remain failed at coverage with 1008/1010 passes, one failed catalog case and one cancellation; pm-web-qdhx owns that unchanged signature. Development-only moderate findings remain with pm-web-c8-glob-advisory. No dependency pin, assertion, deadline or threshold changed. Ready for PR verification; no merge, deployment or publication performed."
  "2026-11-14T12:42:14.935Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Application code and all local validation receipts are complete. PR branch dispatch is waiting for the required orchestrator CI window, which was extended while this task waited. Application code, assertions, deadlines and thresholds are unchanged during the wait. Keep the existing full-release failures and separate downstream passes as recorded; this dispatch delay is not a code or validation failure."
  "2026-11-14T13:29:26.797Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"PR 331 read-only review identified three in-scope regressions to fix: the shared footer starts below the full-height application; stylesheet and service-worker cache keys need the footer revision; and the placement assertion must parse structure rather than match closing-tag text. Reclaiming this item for those corrections. Review threads remain untouched for the orchestrator. Existing full-release catalog failures stay recorded separately."
  "2026-11-14T13:53:58.907Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Review correction passes all 3 native Chromium regressions with no skips. Footer is now a direct child of the common flex shell, outside both hidden screens, and remains visible without outer-page scrolling in 6 initial application viewport/theme combinations. HTML and the emitted service-worker precache use /styles.css?v=22. The DOM oracle rejects a nested lookalike admitted by the old closing-tag regex. Four independent behavioral reversions each fail exactly one browser test: viewport declarations, DOM ancestry, HTML stylesheet key, and emitted worker key (rebuilt before proof). Restoring source and rebuilding passes 3/3. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication (373 sources) and documentation gates pass. No review thread was replied to, resolved or reacted to."
  "2026-11-14T13:55:40.574Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Updated frontend, cache and workflow checks pass 81/81 with zero skips, including service-worker mutation queue and generated scripts; test TypeScript compilation also passes. The 3 native-browser regressions pass separately. Initial head 5e411154ec297b8d31297a94e41422a29bb6076e CI (Node 22/26) and CodeQL were queued during the bounded observation window; run links are in this item. The viewport/cache/DOM review fix will supersede that head and requires fresh CI, not approval inferred from queued, neutral or skipped checks. Final packed consumers are being revalidated against the corrected UI bytes; the original full-suite catalog failure receipts remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-14T14:14:12.318Z",codex-maker-links-1114,"Final corrected UI artifact passes packed acceptance 4/4 (npm/Bun current and minimum hosts), plus 8 permission launchers. SHA-256 1de70868d24bdbc11f9d9f7fd60ecc88cb3cc2968dfcaba7ef57527db880c036; dry-pack contains 513 files. Latest local validation: 81 related tests and 3 native-browser regressions pass, test compilation/typecheck/lint/zero-duplication/documentation pass. Independent revert proofs fail one browser case each for viewport layout, ancestry, HTML key and rebuilt worker key; restoration passes 3/3. Fixes map to PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c63eKVH, PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c63eKVJ and PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c63eKVM. Threads were not replied to, resolved or reacted to. Initial-head CI run 43599128417 is cancelled; CodeQL 43599128286 succeeded only on that prior head. Final fix needs fresh CI; no queued, skipped, neutral or cancelled result is approval. Initial full local npm/Bun release attempts remain failed at the unchanged catalog deadline/ENOTDIR signature (1008 pass, one fail, one cancelled each); the corrected UI has the targeted and packed evidence above. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-14T20:20:37.343Z",codex-followups-1114,"PR 331 follow-up: add an actual JavaScript-enabled first-visit browser case at 740x360. It boots the auth screen from a synthetic unauthenticated session, lets the shipped notice script show the banner, checks login and registration geometry and scroll reachability for both footer links. Run the new test on the unchanged styles first, then restore height:auto in the existing auth-specific rule and bump that CSS request key. Keep the signed-in fixed-height shell and its existing viewport tests."
  "2026-11-14T20:24:04.864Z",codex-followups-1114,"Regression proof: the new JavaScript-enabled 740x360 first-visitor test fails on the prior CSS with login: auth form must end before the cookie notice. Auth-only height:auto fixes it while the signed-in 100dvh shell stays intact. Both login and registration now place the form, footer and live cookie notice in order; both maker links remain reachable by scrolling. Bumped cookie-consent.css request key to v3. Linked browser/brand tests pass 6/6, adjacent consent/legal/static-script/isolation/replay tests pass 54/54, with zero failures/skips. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run build:frontend pass. Full release and capacity gates remain in CI."
